    "problems": "The attack requires access to both pre- and post-unlearning checkpoints or retained logits, limiting applicability. Results use two default base models and specified datasets; the medical data are synthetic. The reported standard deviation for A-ESR across three unlearning runs is <0.01 and is omitted from the table. The study does not compare the paired-checkpoint attack with a chance baseline.",
    "rows_left_out": "Table 1 and Table 2 also report Rouge-L(R) and A-ESR0.9; these metric-specific rows are not included here. Other relevant attack results are in Table 3 (approximate unlearning), Table 4 (LoRA fine-tuning on Phi-1.5), Table 5 (Mixtral-8x7B-Instruct), and Table 6 (ETHICIST comparison). Defense results for unrelated data and noisy updates appear in Fig. 10 and Fig. 11; hyperparameter, forgetting-set-size, and epoch sweeps appear in Figs. 3–8. These are omitted to prioritize the main exact-unlearning comparison and the medical dataset extraction results.",
    "untested": [
      {
        "version": "A",
        "parts": "No attack using only the unlearned model; no chance-level MCQ accuracy; no general-ability check beyond retain-set Rouge."
      },
      {
        "version": "B",
